  "body": "## Behavior changes\r\n- Screenshots now use the layout engine: `Page.captureScreenshot`, BiDi screenshots and `fetch --dump png` draw boxes where `getBoundingClientRect` puts them. `--png-mode reader` gives the old one-column text rendering. The agent's `/screenshot` keeps `reader` by default (`mode=` to change it). PDF is always `reader`.\r\n- `Page.getLayoutMetrics` now comes from the layout engine, and the root container is as wide as the viewport instead of a fixed 1920px.\r\n- CORS: a `*` in `Access-Control-Allow-Headers` now covers `Authorization`, as every browser does.\r\n- A response with no declared charset that is clearly not UTF-8 is decoded as windows-1252.\r\n- CDP: `DOM`, `CSS`, `Accessibility` and `Input` commands (other than `enable`/`disable`) now fail on the startup placeholder target.\r\n\r\n## Serve / CLI\r\n- `--cdp-allow-timezone-override`: lets `Emulation.setTimezoneOverride` change the time zone used by `Date` and `Intl`. The zone is shared by the whole process. Without the flag, the command is accepted and ignored with a warning\r\n- `--png-mode layout|reader` for `fetch --dump png`\r\n- `agent --temperature <FLOAT>`\r\n\r\n## Layout\r\n- Padding and `box-sizing`\r\n- Margins move boxes horizontally; `margin: 0 auto` centers, `margin-left: auto` pushes right\r\n- `gap`, `row-gap` and `column-gap` in flex layouts; text between flex items counts as an item\r\n- `bottom` sizes a fixed or absolute box\r\n- Every `z-index` value is used for hit testing\r\n- `html` and `body` take their declared height (`height: 100%`); `canvas` and `video` without a size are 300×150\r\n- Every `display` value is tracked, for layout and `getComputedStyle`\r\n\r\n## New Web APIs\r\n- `navigator.clipboard.readText()` and `writeText()` (a per-session buffer, never the system clipboard; secure contexts only)\r\n- `HTMLMediaElement` timeline: `duration`, a `currentTime` that advances while playing, seeking, `ended`, `loop` and the matching events (nothing is decoded or played)\r\n- `ReadableStreamDefaultReader.closed`\r\n- `OffscreenCanvas` is an `EventTarget` (Flutter web apps now start)\r\n\r\n## Web API behavior / fixes\r\n- CSS rules inside an `@supports` block are applied when the condition holds\r\n- Streams: `pull()` waits for `start()` and for its own previous call, and runs again when a read waits (fixes Next.js 16 prefetch streams); `cancel()` handles a returned promise, and both `tee()` branches share one cancel promise\r\n- XML parsing keeps namespace declarations (`xmlns`, `xmlns:b`) and creates `CDATASection` nodes\r\n\r\n## CDP\r\n- `Emulation.setTimezoneOverride` applies the zone (with `--cdp-allow-timezone-override`) and rejects unknown zone ids\r\n- `LP.detectForms` `includeValidation` option: returns each field's validation message\r\n\r\n## BiDi\r\n- `script.addPreloadScript`\r\n- `script.getRealms`\r\n- `browsingContext.captureScreenshot`\r\n- `browsingContext.handleUserPrompt`, and a new `lp.handleUserPrompt`, like CDP's `LP.handleJavaScriptDialog`\r\n\r\n## Tools / MCP\r\n- `detectForms` `includeValidation` option: returns each field's validation message, so an agent can read why a form was rejected\r\n\r\n## Performance / memory\r\n- Startup no longer loads every CA certificate twice (about 30% of a simple `fetch`)\r\n- Semantic tree dumps register far fewer nodes (HTML spec: 672k → 314k)\r\n- `getBoundingClientRect` and other `DOMRect` returns skip the identity map\r\n- Less memory for the identity map, cloned attributes, inline scripts, selectors, node lists and PNG rendering (drawn 128 rows at a time)\r\n- Faster style matching: better `:where()` bucketing, an ancestor bloom filter, and selectors that can never match are dropped\r\n- A class change that can't move a box no longer clears the layout cache",
